Subject: [PATCH] misc: add H432B GPS power/reset sequencing

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board power sequencing]

Keep receiver power and reset sequencing separate from the UART interface.
The board supply remains enabled during sleep and is released on shutdown.

---
--- a/drivers/misc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/misc/Kconfig
@@ -1,0 +2,9 @@
+config H432B_GPS_POWER
+	bool "H432B GPS power/reset sequencing"
+	depends on OF && GPIOLIB && REGULATOR
+	help
+	  Enable the board GPS rail and release reset after 100 ms.
+	  Retain power across sleep; remove it on detach and system shutdown.
+	  Receiver communication uses the separately configured UART.
+	  This is board wiring support rather than a GNSS protocol driver.
+
--- a/drivers/misc/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/misc/Makefile
@@ -1,0 +2,1 @@
+obj-$(CONFIG_H432B_GPS_POWER) += h432b-gps-power.o
